WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:02.005
Sagittarius A star.

00:02.705 --> 00:05.203
Nobody can see this black hole itself.

00:05.653 --> 00:15.458
Astronomers watched a star go round it, once every sixteen years, at millions of kilometres an hour, and worked out what it must be circling.

00:15.908 --> 00:25.037
Then eight radio observatories, working as one telescope the size of the Earth, made this picture: glowing gas, and a shadow in the middle.
